The dedication above covers the original work in this repository. Two
vendored single-header libraries carry their own terms, and those terms
travel with the code. They are not ours to release.

  stb_image.h
    Sean Barrett and contributors.
    Dual-licensed: public domain (Unlicense) OR MIT. Either may be used.
    https://github.com/nothings/stb

  simplewebp.h
    Google Inc., Miku AuahDark, and contributors.
    BSD 3-Clause. Requires that the copyright notice, this list of
    conditions, and the disclaimer be retained in redistributions.
    The full text and the WebM codec patent grant are inside the header.
    https://github.com/MikuAuahDark/simplewebp

Original to this project and covered by the dedication above:

  orb_recorder.c          application core
  platform.h              the OS abstraction seam
  platform_win32.c        Windows implementation
  platform_win32_video.c  Windows H.264/AAC via Media Foundation + WASAPI
  platform_x11.c          Linux / X11 implementation
  gif.h                   GIF89a writer (LZW encoder, tree dictionary).
                          The container layout and LZW algorithm follow the
                          published GIF89a specification (Appendix E); the
                          encoder structure is conventional and mirrors the
                          well-known gif-h layout by Charlie Tangora
                          (public domain).
  gif_reader.h            GIF89a reader (LZW decoder, frame compositing)
  png_write.h             PNG writer

GLFW is a build dependency, not bundled here. GLFW is zlib/libpng licensed.

The LZW patents expired worldwide in 2004.
